  "body": "Found by the review of PR #65 (#62). With #62, a bar off the world origin passes once G54 is moved onto it, but `cross_drill` (crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs ~1760) computes `stock_r` about world (0, 0), not about the work offset, so cross-hole clearance and standoff distances come out wrong. Its comment also implies a downstream refusal for parts the axis fit can't read, and the cross-drill path has none.\n\nDone means: cross_drill measures about the same spindle the post uses (work-offset origin, world Z) and refuses by name a part the fit can't read; pinned by a test with a bar off the world origin under a moved G54.",
